From cc46dab0930714634aba894abae801740a824578 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:37:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] Eden (Doris): texture cleanup that keeps GPU drawings
 (setting, on by default)

Build 12's report: Eden's texture garbage collector starts at 40% of the GPU
memory budget (1.6 GiB of 4 GiB on Snapdragon 8 Gen 2), counted over all the
app's GPU memory. TotK in heavy areas sits at 1.7-2.2 GiB, so the collector
ran every frame: 1500-2900 textures removed and 2000-3800 re-uploaded every 10
seconds (about 10% of the GPU thread), up to 2059 copies back to guest memory
in 10 seconds (each one waits for the GPU to finish everything: the GPU thread
spent 19.5 ms of every frame waiting, 15 fps), and 10-124 textures the GPU had
drawn thrown away every 10 seconds (rebuilt later from stale memory: flicker).

Doris collection (Texture memory cleanup = Doris):
- starts at 2.4 GiB (at least 512 MiB below the critical level, never below
  Eden's own threshold);
- textures must sit unused for 300 frames (120 under pressure, 20 when
  critical) instead of 50/25/10;
- textures the GPU drew into are only removed when memory is critical (Eden's
  behaviour then); looking at them uses a separate budget so they can't block
  the collection of others.

Also: hand work to the Vulkan worker every 8 draws instead of 4 (each hand-off
to a sleeping worker is a futex call: 4.5% of the GPU thread in build 12).
Submits stay every 512 draws, as in Eden.
